## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design edge routing with policy-driven gating and cross-DC deployment, plus observability and security concerns in docker-dca.

## Key Concepts

- TLS termination at the edge with Nginx
- Central policy engine (OPA) integration
- Per-tenant feature flag evaluation
- Cross-DC routing semantics
- Observability with Prometheus and OTEL

## Code Example

```rego
package featureflag.allow
default allow = false
allow {
  input.tenant == "tenant-A"
  input.flag == "new_feature"
}
```

```nginx
# Nginx map-based routing example
http {
  map $http_x_feature_flag $upstream {
    default http://api_v1;
    "new_feature" http://api_v2;
  }
  server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    location /api/ { proxy_pass $upstream; }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement cache invalidation for policy decisions?
- How would you test the canary routing?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests depth of cross-DC security, dynamic policy loading, and automated risk controls in a real-world Docker DC architecture.

## Key Concepts

- SPIFFE/SVIDs with Vault
- WASM-based per-tenant policy engine
- Edge verifier sidecar for SVID validation
- Canary deployments and automatic rollback
- Cross-DC routing and observability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: load tenant policy from broker and validate SVID before calling app
async function handleRequest(req){
  const svid = await verifySVID(req.headers['spiffe']);
  const(policy) = await loadPolicyFromBroker(req.tenant);
  if(!policy.allows(req)) throw new Error('Access denied');
  return proxyToApp(req);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you debug a scenario where Vault rotation invalidates existing SVIDs mid-rollout?
- What metrics and traces would you collect to enforce the 25% canary SLA thresholds across DCs?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end trust from image provenance to runtime policy enforcement, plus canary control and rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Content Trust/Notary for image provenance
- SPIFFE/SVIDs via Vault for mTLS
- OPA policies loaded via Docker Config
- Sigver sidecar for per-request validation
- Canary rollout with latency/error thresholds and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo example: verify image signature before starting app
async function verifySignature(image) {
  const sig = await notary.verify(image);
  if (!sig || !sig.valid) throw new Error('invalid image');
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle signature revocation and key rotation in this setup?
- How would you scale the sigver and policy sidecars across nodes?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical skills in dynamic per-tenant API version routing, assessing candidates' knowledge of Redis-backed routing state, Traefik dynamic configuration, and Docker-based edge proxies across distributed infrastructure.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant version routing
- Redis-backed configuration store (tenant_id → api_version)
- Traefik dynamic configuration via Docker provider
- Sidecar pattern for pushing configuration updates
- Multi-datacenter consistency and TLS edge handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Sidecar that watches Redis and updates Traefik rules
async function syncRoutes(redis, docker) {
  const routes = await redis.hgetall('tenant:versions');
  for (const [tenantId, version] of Object.entries(routes)) {
    await updateTraefikRule(docker, tenantId, version);
  }
}
```
